@theme exams
// Writer-commons, themes batch. From content/arcs/outlines.md, "The struggle themes". Any department, either shift.
// Fill-ins assumed: {home} a place ("Lisk"), {family} with "my" ("my gran"), {hobby} an activity ("painting"),
// {since} a length of time ("five years"). A beat that names one lists it in needs:, so people without it skip it.

== beat 1
tone: light
hint: Quick question. What comes after step three? Kidding. Unless you know.
mem: studying
them: Don't mind me. I'm revising at dinner. It's that or dream about it.   [laugh]
them: My exam's coming. I've read this page six times. I couldn't tell you what's on it.
? choice
* Want me to test you?   flavour:practical mem:tested
  them: Yes. No. Yes. Go easy. No, don't go easy.
* You'll be fine. Probably.   flavour:cheer
  them: Probably! The confidence. I'll take it.   [laugh]
them: Back to page six. Page six, my old friend.

== beat 2
tone: heartfelt
hint: Got a minute? I need to say a thing out loud so it stops being so big.
mem: afraid
them: The exam's next week. I'm scared I'll fail it. Properly scared.   [sigh]
them: Everyone knows I sat it. If I fail, they'll be kind about it. That's worse.
them: I just want to be good at this. I want them to be right to have picked me.
? choice
* They picked you because you're good. I've seen it.   flavour:cheer mem:seen
  them: Have you? Really? Say it again. Slowly.   [laugh]
  + them: You have, haven't you. You've watched me work. All right. That helps more than the book does.
* What would failing actually mean?   flavour:listen mem:means
  them: A retake. Three months. Nobody would mind but me. Huh. Said out loud it's smaller.
* Quiz me every night till then.   flavour:practical mem:nightly
  them: Every night. Even when I'm grumpy. Especially when I'm grumpy.
them: Thanks. I'm still scared. Just less on my own about it.

== beat 3
tone: resolution
hint: Guess. Go on. Guess what happened.
mem: result
them: I sat it. I came out shaking and I couldn't remember a single question.
them: Passed. Well. Mostly passed. Passed enough. Close enough to celebrate.   [laugh]
them: And if I hadn't, you'd have been there. I knew that walking in. It helped.
? choice
* I knew you would.   flavour:cheer
  them: You did. You said so every night. I'm going to say it about you one day.
  + them: You did, every single night. Right. Tea's on me. Biscuits too. All the biscuits.
* How do you feel?   flavour:listen mem:feel
  them: Tired. Proud. A bit sick. Mostly proud. Is that allowed?
them: Next one's in a year. Don't remind me. Do remind me. In about eleven months.
